summary:
servd has no head office entity today. "Head office" exists in six separate pieces, and none of them knows about the others:
(a) `Department.isHeadOffice`, a per-company badge;
(b) `Position.tenantCostShareCents` plus a free-text `costShareNote`;
(c) `TenantContribution` (category `head_office`), a monthly transfer between two companies that is used for planning only and never reaches the ledger. Seed data: GS Foods carries the 800k/month head office payroll and the JV sends 500k back;
(d) the brand P&L line "Head office (unallocated)", which is only the untagged overhead inside ONE company;
(e) multi-company logins through `TenantMember`, the "head-office staffer" pattern. These users get write scope over every company they belong to and an "All companies" read view, and have one `HrEmployee` record per company (decision 31);
(f) `FleetAgreement`, the only deliberate crossing between companies, with `RiderJobEvent` stamped with both companies "for a future cost split".

Payroll is per company: `HrPayrollRun` → `hr/ledger.ts` `postPayrollAccrual` posts to that company's own books. Head-office pay therefore sits wherever the person is employed (today GS Foods), and the other companies' share is only a number in planning screens.

Missing pieces:
- The chart of accounts has no intercompany (due to / due from) accounts.
- The allocation engine refuses to cross companies.
- The team tree and HOD approval step stop at the company boundary.
- CEO approvals are spread across five or more screens. None of them can be handed to someone else.

Recommendation: make each head office a Tenant of kind `head_office`, so it has its own HR, payroll and ledger. Add one link table, HeadOfficeCompany, which the CEO edits. HO staff get read access across the HO's companies, worked out from that link (not copied into membership rows). A monthly recharge run, built by extending the existing allocation engine, posts matching intercompany entries in the head office's books and in each company's books. This replaces `TenantContribution(head_office)`, `Department.isHeadOffice` and the per-position cost-share notes rather than sitting beside them.
